# Counter-example: a lang:AnalysisOutput that names NO lang:CanonicalizationProfile
# through lang:analyzedUnderProfile — an orphan analyzer result whose comparability
# claim is fabricated because the substrate it was folded under is undeclared. The
# analyzer-stratum twin of ingestion-unattributed-engine-claim.ttl (an engine reading
# with no vantage): here a fold key enters the graph with no cited profile at all, so
# lang:ProfileAttributionConstraint MUST reject it (fires lang:UnattributedAnalysisProfile
# via the sh:sparql of the projected lang:ProfileAttributionConstraintProceduralConstraintShape,
# whose FILTER NOT EXISTS body finds no analyzedUnderProfile edge to a stage-declaring
# profile). The node carries only its type, so no other lang shape is in scope.

@prefix lang:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/lang/> .

ex:orphanFoldKey a lang:AnalysisOutput .
